You have Charles Bonnet syndrome. This means you may see visual images that are not actually present, such as patterns, shapes, small figures or faces, or even detailed scenes. These are caused by the brain responding to reduced visual input from the eyes when vision loss has occurred. \
\
Importantly, this is not a mental health condition. Many people with reduced vision experience this, and the images are typically recognized as not real.\
